From 0a5ba051b8812e874f6651326a6a9400d1712f2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] redfin 1034: USB Ethernet fast path (batched bulk IN, sub-ms
 event polls), off by default

Phone -> PC TCP ran at 1.23 MB/s, about one 1514-byte frame per 1.2 ms:
ud_tx_kick_locked starts one single-TRB transfer per frame and only queues
the next after that transfer's XferComplete, which ud_thread sees at its
next 1 ms poll (assert_wait_deadline with default timer leeway).

kern.sweet_usb_txbatch N (boot sweetusbtxb=N, 2..16) puts up to N queued
frames in one StartTransfer, one unchained TRB per frame (each ends in a
short packet = one ECM frame), LST|IOC on the last, in separate
contiguous kernel memory; TX queue cap 64. kern.sweet_usb_poll_us US (boot
sweetusbpollus=US, 50..1000) polls the event buffer every US us with
TIMEOUT_URGENCY_SYS_CRITICAL while TX is in flight or within 5 ms of an
event. Both 0 = the old behaviour. Counters kern.sweet_usb_tx_frames,
_tx_xfers, _tx_drops, _rx_frames.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_013SvAC47UfuRo4oy9dg357w
